{"id": "swebq0166", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 1.44, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2128, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Orville Wright;Wilbur Wright", "query": "who were wright brothers?", "transcript": "Who are Wright brothers?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The Wright brothers were Orville and Wilbur Wright. They were American inventors and pioneers of aviation. Together, they designed, built, and flew the world's first successful airplane. Their most famous flight took place in Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, in December 1903. The Wright brothers are credited with inventing, building, and flying the world's first sustained, controlled, powered heavier-than-air human flight. Their work laid the foundation for modern aviation.", "answer_ms": 2188}
