{"id": "swebq0196", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2857, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Pacific Time Zone;UTC-8", "query": "when do they change the time in california?", "transcript": "When do they change the time in California?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The time in California changes twice a year. In the spring it shifts forward an hour during the daylight saving time change which usually happens on the second Sunday of March. Then in the fall it shifts back an hour typically on the first Sunday of November as we return to standard time.", "answer_ms": 1219}
{"id": "swebq0199", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 1.81, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1492, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Édouard Manet;Paul Cézanne;Henri Rousseau;Paul Gauguin;Sara Murphy;Diego Velázquez;Jean Auguste Dominique Ingres;Eugène Delacroix;Alfred Jarry;Francisco Goya", "query": "who influenced picasso art?", "transcript": "Who influenced Picasso?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Pablo Picasso was influenced by many artists, but perhaps the most significant was his close friend and fellow artist, Georges Braque. Braque's work in still life painting and his interest in texture deeply influenced Picasso's development of Cubism.", "answer_ms": 1039}
{"id": "swebq0202", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.6, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4483, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Kohler", "query": "where are kohler sinks manufactured?", "transcript": "Where are Kohler sinks manufactured?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Kohler sinks are manufactured in several locations around the world. Some, particularly enameled cast iron models, come from Kohler, Wisconsin, USA, while others may be made in countries like China, India, or Mexico depending on the specific product line. To find out exactly where a particular sink was made, you can usually check the packaging, label, or consult Kohler’s official specifications for that model.", "expert_answer": "Kohler sinks are manufactured in multiple locations worldwide, depending on the model and material. Some Kohler sinks—especially enameled cast iron products—are made in Kohler, Wisconsin, USA, while other models may be produced in countries such as China, India, or Mexico.\n\nFor the exact origin of a specific sink, check the product packaging, label, or Kohler’s specification sheet for that model.", "expert_latency_s": 6.75, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1908}
