{"id": "swebq0226", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.51, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1486, "eot_read_ms": 18, "reference_answer": "Reflecting telescope", "query": "what was sir isaac newton's inventions?", "transcript": "What was Sir Isaac Newton's inventions?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Sir Isaac Newton didn't invent things in the way we think of modern inventions, like gadgets or machines. But he made some of the most important discoveries in science. He figured out the laws of motion and gravity. For example, he explained why apples fall from trees and how planets move around the sun. So while he didn't \"invent\" something you can hold, his ideas changed how we understand the world.", "answer_ms": 1687}
